  "body": "- \u2611\ufe0f I understand it is strictly prohibited to use AI to write PR description\r\n\r\n- Implements the int8 half of [mlx#4627](https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx/issues/4627) to stage the matmul's weights and activations as int8 instead of dequantizing to fp16; the fp8 half will follow in a separate PR. Enabled with the environment variable `MLX_QMM_INT8`, **off by default; stock path unchanged.**\r\n\r\n- Validation lists: Speed improvements for quantized matmul. Measured on 36969c094, the PR is now rebased to a21f892a. \r\n\r\n| Scenario | M5 10-core GPU | M6 12-core GPU |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| int8 prefill, N=8192 | 1.392x | 1.349x |\r\n| int8 prefill, N=4096 | 1.450x | 1.413x |\r\n| int8 prefill, N=2048 | 1.467x | 1.420x |\r\n| int8 prefill, N=512 | 1.531x | 1.363x |\r\n| int8 decode | 0.999x, steps bit-identical | 1.004x, steps bit-identical |\r\n\r\n_(prefill M=2048, decode M=1)_\r\n\r\n- Exactness: with the switch off (default), every single-op cell is bit-identical to the unmodified build (12/12); decode steps are bit-identical on both hosts; the upstream `test_quantized.py` passes in every build, including the three new tests.\r\n\r\n- Single-op table: Speed improvements (M = 2048, bf16 input, switch off over on, median of nine pairs; modes 1 / 2 / 4), as measured on base 36969c094.\r\n\r\n| shape | M6 mode 1 / 2 / 4 | M5 mode 1 / 2 / 4 |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| q/o 4096 x 4096 | 1.33x / 1.60x / 1.49x| 1.33x / 1.68x / 1.56x | \r\n| gate/up 4096 x 12288 | 1.31x / 1.63x / 1.52x | 1.35x / 1.64x / 1.51x | \r\n| down 12288 x 4096 | 1.49x / 1.85x / 1.73x |  1.38x / 1.66x / 1.52x | \r\n| thin N 5120 x 48 | 1.14x / 1.15x / 1.17x |  1.28x / 1.27x / 1.28x | \r\n\r\n- Serving test using Qwen 27B (M5 Pro; `lmstudio-community/Qwen3.8-27B-MLX-4bit`, affine 4-bit g64, oMLX): prefill 1.44-1.51x at a measurable quality cost, depending on policy:\r\n\r\n| Policy (all 4-bit affine g64, head stock, >= 64 rows) | Cold prefill / stock speed| Quality, relative PPL, worst domain (literature) | \r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Full staged int8 (attention mode 2; MLP/GDN mode 4) | 1.436x geomean (1.408 / 1.490 / 1.411); 1.511x in a later session; 1.456x against the release wheel with native kernels | +2.08% [+1.74, +2.43]; science +1.53%, math +0.65%, code +0.10% |\r\n| Attention stock (MLP/GDN mode 4) | 1.466x | +0.85% / upper +1.13% | \r\n| Attention + MLP stock (GDN mode 4) | 1.106x | +0.31% / upper +0.48% | \r\n\r\n- Quality impact: the 27B worst-domain upper bound (full staged int8, +2.08%) fails the research's own +1% bar, literature and science degrade, math and code are near parity; task-level parity was not tested (no GSM8K or coding suite). For the smaller Qwen3-8B on the same path we measured similar prefill speedups, with a +0.56 / +0.76 / +0.59 / +0.18% relative PPL impact (worst upper 0.92%) on base commit. **The mechanism is opt-in and off by default**; per-layer policy lives in the serving harness, not in MLX.\r\n\r\n- Note: the numbers are from before #4682 which is now in main and makes M6 stock slower at large M, while flat/faster on M5. This is a separate issue, which I may report separately. This PR is not addressing that issue. \r\n\r\n- Benchmark-script: qmm_8bit_bench.py _(attached in comment to PR)_\r\n\r\n```sh\r\npython qmm_8bit_bench.py --save-hashes h.json    # run on an unpatched build first\r\npython qmm_8bit_bench.py --check-hashes h.json   # then on this PR\r\n```\r\n\r\n- Selector rules for new GEMM QMM path: \r\n    - Environment variable `MLX_QMM_INT8`: default `0` (off); set to `1`, `4` or `2` to enable, most to least precise; other values are ignored; read through the config module so first read caches the environment.\r\n    - quantized.cpp dispatch (affine, 2-D transposed weights, int8-capable hardware, K % 64 == 0, M >= 64; bits > 1, so 1-bit weights always use the stock path). Also K/64 <= 1024 (K \u2264 65,536), group sizes 32/64/128, non-batched. (the gate is a coverage choice, not a small-M gain claim)\r\n    - In essence, these dispatch rules accelerate only affine-quantized linear layers during prefill on NAX hardware (M5/M6 today) while decode is unchanged.\r\n\r\n- SIMD fix (18b7e0eaa) to remove undefined behavior for partial SIMD groups in affine_qmm_i8_quantize_x (padded threadgroup), sweep over 624 cells/host across 13 K values (9 not multiples of 32) are bit-identical; no arithmetic change; gates/tests unchanged\r\n\r\n- `test_quantized.py`: 58 OK on stock build, 62 OK on head build with 1 skipped. JIT build (MLX_METAL_JIT=ON) on the pushed head sweep bit-identical; JIT and non-JIT outputs agree.\r\n\r\n- FP8: This PR adds only the int8 path. Staging QMM on fp8 instead of int8 (which additionally exploits the M6 fp8 lanes) will follow in a separate PR. \r\n\r\n- AI usage disclosure: \r\nWritten by me (human) and I understand it is strictly prohibited to use AI to write PR description. Agents did assist in providing the solution, performing the measurements and preparing the data tables. ",
